 "tags": ["look"],
 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "The picture received as a slow scan television image over radio, the way pictures come down from the space station: it builds up line by line, leans over when the receiver clock is off with the dark sync stripe running diagonally through it, jumps sideways where a sync pulse was missed, and picks up coloured streaks where the signal fades and diagonal stripes from a whistling carrier.",
